A||||5||William||OK, I'm ready to talk about my Fiero weekend.||||1||
Z||000000||William||03-01-2001||01:49 AM||||Well, it was quite a weekend! My interior project has gone very well until the past weekend. I had taken an extra day off to get more done on the car. The carpet had arrived and the firewall was getting recovered. I started with the firewall. Against the advice of mr mike, I decided to completely glue the vinyl to the firewall rather than let it foat on top and it dimpled all up as he said it would. The 3m spray glue I used was way too lumpy. I ruined the black vinyl he had sent me, as well as my fire wall. I spent the rest of the day pulling apart boneyard Fieros looking for a usable firewall and then was robbed by owner for an amount of money that I'm ashamed to discuss. Later, I seached all night for black vinyl with no luck and ended up with black felt from walmart. The felt looks fantastic but with the damaged items, the firewall became very expensive to do. The next day, I installed the carpet. This task went much better so things were looking up! Next, it was time to dye the tan seat belts black. I'll just say, NEVER TRY TO DO THAT! :-( At this point,I figured I would make myself feel better by installing some nice new leather! I grabbed my MR Mikes leather E boot and put that puppy on. It was beatiful and William was pleased. I next installed the rear and bottom trim panels so the seats could go back in. As I stood back and admired my work, I noticed a nice round hole in the e boot that I had just installed. I was in shock. How the #%$@ did I do that? I was so careful and I still can't determine how it happened. At this point I was extremely mad and upset. Instead of cooling off I proceeded to cut a strip of rubber that I needed using a razor knife when...Slip! Yep, it happened. A layed my chest open with a foot long gash. As the seats were still sitting in the yard and the interior needed to be wrapped up, there was NO time for sitting in the emergency room on a Sunday evening. Using pads and duct tape, I patched my chest back together and got the seats back in. I then refused to think about Fieros until tonight.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||03-01-2001||02:32 AM||||William, sorry to hear you cut yourself and I hope you are feeling better. <BR>One lesson learned by me that when a pro tells you to do something a certain way, he knows better. He's been there and done that and he also learned the hard way. <BR>Good luck on getting the rest done.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||03-01-2001||08:34 AM||||you sound like me when i take on a project, whatever it be.  Get frustrated, and ending up hurting myself. I;ve got a few battle scars from stupid things like that.<P>hope it heals okay||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||03-01-2001||08:57 AM||||Dude, hope both you and the car are okay!<P>I know how you feel.  I've swapped plenty of blood and sweat with my Fiero, and I've only had it since January!  That's what I get for buying one that will require a cradle drop for repairs (but at least I knew this going into it).  I still have a garage covered in what used to be a whole Fiero waiting for my parts from the Fiero Store to show up.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||03-01-2001||10:10 AM||||Good God William, I'm glad you're ok. I totally understand the anger thing though, I'm just lucky I've never slice myself open like that. I've busted a few knuckles though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
